# data
data/raw/
data/curated/
*.parquet
*.csv
*.db

# ...except the real-price cache, which is committed on purpose. Every report
# citing real data records a fingerprint of the prices it used; that fingerprint
# is worthless if the prices are not in the repository. Yahoo restates adjusted
# history when corporate actions are reprocessed, so a rerun months from now
# would otherwise silently use different data and produce different numbers with
# no way to tell that is what happened. 568KB is a cheap price for reproducibility.
!data_cache/
!data_cache/*.parquet

# The SEC event cache, committed for the same reason as the prices: every
# event result is pinned to the filings it used, and EDGAR accessions are
# immutable, so a committed copy is a permanent record rather than a snapshot
# of a moving target.
!data_cache/edgar/
!data_cache/edgar/*.parquet

# ...but not the raw submissions dumps. Unlike Yahoo, EDGAR never restates: an
# accession number returns the same bytes forever, so the raw pages can be
# refetched identically at any time and committing 9MB of them buys nothing.
# The derived parquets above are the pinned artifacts.
data_cache/edgar/submissions_*.json
data_cache/edgar/company_tickers.json

# The decision journal is the record, not a build artifact. Entries are
# predictions made before the outcome was known, and they are only evidence if
# they are committed at the time rather than reconstructed later.
!journal/
!journal/*.json

# secrets
.env
config/secrets.yaml
*.key

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# os
.DS_Store

# build artifacts
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
